-- statement:
--   An auxiliary lemma of the round-six development, published as a separate node because its proof is long or shared.
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `NLogN.HRM`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem NLogN.RM.code_runs (M : MulSpec) (pM : Fin P) (pc : ℕ → Fin P) (hM : MulOK I iprog pM M) :
--       ∀ (p : RM), PrcOK I iprog pc p → ∀ (s : IState HS), p.ok M s →
--       IRuns I iprog (p.code pM pc) s (p.run s) (p.cost M s)
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** Register programs with multiplication calls
--
--   `RM` extends the register programs `RS` by `mul k i j`, which pushes `top j * top i` onto `k`
--   by calling the multiplication procedure `pM` with the calling convention
--
--     `ARG = 55 : a :: b :: L  ↦  (a * b) :: L`,
--
--   all other stacks unchanged.  The cost of a call and the inputs on which it may be used are a
--   parameter `M : MulSpec`; `RM.code_runs` holds whenever the procedure meets `MulOK M`.
